'''''Fundamental Astronomy''''' (1984–2017) is an [[astronomy]] textbook by Finnish author [[:fi:Hannu Karttunen|Hannu Karttunen]]<ref>[http://www.iau.org/administration/membership/individual/7749/ Hannu Karttunen]</ref> of [[University of Turku]]; [[Pekka Kröger]] and [[Heikki Oja]]<ref>[http://www.iau.org/administration/membership/individual/5165/ Heikki Oja]</ref> of [[University of Helsinki]]; [[Markku Poutanen]]<ref>[http://www.fgi.fi/fgi/contact/person/markku-poutanen Markku Poutanen]</ref> of [[Finnish Geodetic Institute]]; and [[Karl Johan Donner]]<ref>[http://www.iau.org/administration/membership/individual/7342/ Karl J. Donner]</ref> of [[University of Helsinki]]. The first edition was published in Finnish by Ursa, [[Helsinki]], 1984, and later published in English by [[Springer (publisher)|Springer]]. The 6th edition was published in 2017 ({{ISBN|978-3-662-53044-3}}; previous editions were published in 2007, 2003, 1996, 1994 and 1987). It contains 548 pages and is illustrated with more than 419 images, including 34 color plates. There are many pages on the [[Solar System]], the [[Milky Way]], galaxies, and cosmology.

Aimed at the [[science]] student market, this textbook is both for undergraduates and for graduates just beginning their courses who are looking for an overview. It covers the whole field of modern [[astronomy]]. While emphasizing both the astronomical concepts and the underlying physical principles, the text provides a basis for more further studies in the astronomical sciences.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783662530443|title=Fundamental Astronomy &#124; SpringerLink}}</ref>

