'''Advanced Placement''' ('''AP''') '''Physics 1: Algebra Based'''<ref>{{Cite web |title=AP Physics 1: Algebra-Based Course – AP Central {{!}} College Board |url=https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/courses/ap-physics-1 |access-date=2024-09-04 |website=apcentral.collegeboard.org |language=en}}</ref> (also known as '''AP Physics 1''') is a year-long introductory [[physics]] course administered by the [[College Board]] as part of its [[Advanced Placement]] program. It is intended to proxy a one-semester algebra-based university course in [[mechanics]]. Along with [[AP Physics 2]], the first AP Physics 1 exam was administered in 2015.

